title Caravan allay -- the reader who was told says whether the second look puts the matter to rest
prompt Autonomous loop -- Standfast on reds, then the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first, council rota doc by lap index, condense REMEMBER when a set completes, and send each finished increment as its own signed round.
think Standfast first. Every living row in crux/REDS.md reads CLOSED -- %96, %97, %81, %83, %84 -- so no red books this lap's allocation and the constructive queue is open.
think Council rota by lap index: 1421 logs on disk, 1421 mod 27 = 17, which is context/LEXICON.md. Deep-read: the project names, the loop gates, the module and aspect pattern, the core stack, the archive and digest tiers, the referential namespace, the type-marks and the crossing. It paid immediately -- the Comlink tendency's three tests (clear, fun, safe) chose this rung's name, and the Dependent row is the standing example of a molt the arc earned rather than imposed.
think Two doors stood open from the last lap's recommend. Option B, the shared harness, would take the remaining 12,035 carried lines and end both limits the fold refused to cross. The outer loop stood exactly where it was: nothing read whether a second look finally settles the matter. Lindy-first ranks B higher as infrastructure every future rung inherits, yet the finishing edge rules the tie -- A landed one lap ago, the meter carries about six rungs of headroom, and B is a design question (what is the contract between a harness and a rung's report?) that wants its own call rather than an autonomous rewrite across 91 modules. So this lap took the constructive rung and left B named, measured, and one lap closer.
think The name came from the Comlink tendency rather than from a four-letter draw. Candidates weighed and grepped: settle collides 225 times inside caravan alone (the run's own verdict word), rest reads as HTTP and as Keaton's own rest, accept collides with the socket sense. allay is clear, warm, plain, and appears nowhere in any .rye in the tree.
think The shape is apprise's shape one tier out. There a plan carried a finding and never learned its worth, and suffice answered it; here a plan carries a second look home and never learns whether it allayed anything. So the rung is built exactly as suffice was: the reader keeps five bytes in their own box, the run reads them, and the plan copies one byte where the settlement is read.
think Five refusals earned their order by argument. AllayUntold is the moment a reply is read at all -- a run that told nobody has no reply coming. AllaySilent is whether there is a word there. AllayMismatched is the whole point. AllayMiscounted is the honesty of the count. AllayMisrecorded is the record, read back off the wire rather than out of the memory of having written it.
obs Six RED paths proven on metal before any GREEN claim, each by disarming one guard and rebuilding: skip the write and the run refuses AllayMisrecorded; read the telling as never made, AllayUntold; read the reader as having written nothing, AllaySilent; carry a reply about some other telling, AllayMismatched; count one telling both read and unread, AllayMiscounted.
obs The sixth is the planted control -- the write, the run's read-back, the wire fold's three reads and the bare run's one all disarmed at once -- and the selftest printed GREEN while caravan/.allays/plan.rest did not exist at all. Seeing that is what makes the reading back a check rather than decoration.
obs The wire reads what the prose claims: desk.rests holds osrwa, the four bytes of the telling echoed back whole with the reader's own word last, and plan.rest holds the single byte a. The telling itself still stands in the reader's box, since reading a reply opens an answer rather than spending one.
obs An honest RED taught the wire fold its shape. Written the first way, the fold expected a provisioning to sweep the plan's own copy of the word; the rung below had proven the opposite for its own note, and the answer is that a published word survives a provisioning and falls only with the telling it answers -- exactly as suffice's copy falls with the answer it weighs.
obs The tier shift was the one place a mechanical edit lied. Adding a tier to every _run.inner chain by repeated replacement re-matched its own output and pushed some reads six tiers deep; the compiler caught all of it by naming a field that does not exist on the struct it landed on, which is the ladder's carried checks doing their job again.
obs The 70-line ratchet fired on this rung's own growth and was answered rather than carried: seat_the_wire reached 71 lines, so the reader's own words and this lap's own clearing each earned a named function -- seat_the_readers_words and clear_this_laps_notes -- and the ratchet is clear of allay.
obs The fold wall moved with the ladder rather than against it. The meter pinned 523 folded checks; allay folds 39 more as it is written, so the pin stands at 562 and its comment now says the number climbs with each rung and never falls, which makes a drop a regression the wall names on the lap it happens.
loom witness=caravan_allay_witness rungs_green=86 ladder_modules=91 ladder_checks=1154 copied_lines=13830 ceiling=22000 folded_checks=562
file caravan/allay.rye the rung -- the reader's reply read where they wrote it, published where the settlement is read, five refusals by name
file tools/caravan_allay_witness.rish the witness -- the finding, the five refusals, the measured pair, and every note read off the wire outside the run that wrote it
file tools/caravan_suite_witness.rish the choir hears the new rung; roster whole at 86, bijection proven before the singing
file tools/caravan_ladder_copy_witness.rish the fold wall moves to 562, and its comment says why the number climbs
file caravan/README.md the durable record of the rung, beside the fold that made room for it
file active-designing/20260820-131713_caravan-ladder-shared-harness.md a duplicated phrase in the addendum repaired, prose only
file crux/REMEMBER.md the live edge names this rung and the git nib moves with the work
recommend keep-going the arc now corrects a record, carries the correction, hears the answer, records the disagreement, escorts the word, bounds the objection, stands its standing, tells the raiser, reads their reply, carries a live quarrel past the run that heard it, makes the inheriting run answer for it, lets its holder close it, dates it, reads that age aloud, puts a long-standing one before a third hand, reads back what that hand made of it, makes the plan answer that finding on the record, carries the plan's own concession forward, makes the run that inherits it meet it, makes that meeting say what it found, carries that finding home to the reader who won it, reads what that reader makes of it, takes the matter up again when they say it falls short, makes the run that inherits that reopening look, carries what the second look found home, and now reads whether that finally settles it. So the question above is what a plan does with a matter its reader says still stands -- the correspondence has closed one full turn, and nothing yet carries a twice-refused matter anywhere but round again. Beside it option B stands measured and one lap closer: the fold left 12,035 carried lines and two named limits, both of which a harness running a rung's checks against its own report and its own wire would take.
